From 0abd9453538a85c6ddd8b73ca3861d466c41a57d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:57:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(api): render every error response with the error
 envelope

Only the create, workflow and decision handlers produced the documented
{"error": {...}} envelope. Framework-level errors leaked FastAPI defaults:
GET/DELETE 404s and 405s returned {"detail": ...}, request validation
failures returned 422 instead of the contract's 400, and unhandled
exceptions produced plain-text 500s.

Register global handlers for HTTPException, RequestValidationError and
uncaught exceptions. Every error now carries a machine-readable code and
the request's correlation id; 500 responses no longer expose internal
details, which are logged instead. ApiError lets dependencies raise a
specific code (used by the upcoming authentication dependency).
